  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q22-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "22",
    "prompt": "A photograph is 18 cm by 12 cm. It is to be surrounded by a frame of uniform width whose area is equal to the area of the photograph. Find the width of the frame.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$3\\text{ cm}$",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the frame width in centimetres, with $x>0$. The photograph has area $18\\times12=216\\text{ cm}^2$, so the total area is $432\\text{ cm}^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x+18)(2x+12)&=18\\times12+18\\times12\\\\4x^2+60x+216&=432\\\\4x^2+60x-216&=0\\\\x^2+15x-54&=0\\\\(x+18)(x-3)&=0\\\\x&=-18\\text{ or }3\\end{align*}$$\nReject $x=-18$ because the width must be positive. The frame is $3\\text{ cm}$ wide.\nCheck: $(18+6)(12+6)-18\\times12=432-216=216\\text{ cm}^2$, equal to the photograph's area.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 80
  },
